sense, because dawn is when the sun comes back.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's also a fairly common metaphor for a transition, which is rather inherent to the premise of Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut I suppose metaphors are pretentious now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T10:27:05-07:00","id":1084544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1082625-why-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-as-the-title?p=1084524#post1084524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt's also a fairly common metaphor for a transition, which is rather inherent to the premise of Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut I suppose metaphors are pretentious now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;This metaphor and prose is pretentious&quot; != &quot;Metaphors and prose are pretentious.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T12:29:59-07:00","id":1084634,"title":"","content":"Belatedly weighing in...<br /> <br /> I'm actually okay with pretty much nobody in Creation knowing the name of the Scarlet Empress. Outside of like, 1d12 Sidereals and a handful of gods. I mean, if I were in the Empress's position, having just purged Creation of a major Fair Folk invasion and in a position to call myself the Bitch Queen of Creation... Lord knows I'd take on a new name and refuse to acknowledge my old one. And given that she just went through a war, and IIRC she was a soldier of little social standing beforehand...<br /> <br /> Y'know, I'm fine with my table having &quot;When she took the throne, almost nobody knew her name. After she took the name, she called herself the Scarlet Empress. So few people could contradict her that the name stuck&quot;<br /> <br /> Now her ASPECT not being known, at least among the Realm, is a bit harder for me to swallow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:01:55-07:00","id":1084651,"title":"","content":"What is the power of Names in 3e? Could removing her Name from every possible record be a form of protection from Sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:10:56-07:00","id":1084656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1082625-why-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-as-the-title?p=1084634#post1084634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...<br /> Now her ASPECT not being known, at least among the Realm, is a bit harder for me to swallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>As kind of noted upthread, I don't think it's a matter that no one knows. I think that it's a matter that in the general scheme of things of how the world is and what wrodcount is put to, it really doesn't ultimatley matter. It's whatever works for your game, but generally isn't something that needs to be pinned down.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T13:20:47-07:00","id":1084666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1082625-why-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-as-the-title?p=1084651#post1084651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the power of Names in 3e? Could removing her Name from every possible record be a form of protection from Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI have a personal interest in names not being very significant to that kind of magic, beyond a general targeting mechanism that will go by whatever the person happens to call themselves by. After all, we already know what the setting's general sorcery is like, and it doesn't really incorporate a deal with knowing a person's name giving you a special power over them, and the setting in general doesn't really act as though people hide their names.<br /> <br /> \u200bMostly it's a case of how I think many instances of the Exalted lend themselves readily to a cultural perspective that your real name is the one you opt to go by at the time. I get the basis of magic through somebody having an essential name, and even like certain properties featuring it, but I would also like some properties in which it has no power and one can go by whatever they want without any implication that it is somehow less real.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T14:39:05-07:00","id":1084703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1082625-why-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-as-the-title?p=1084634#post1084634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Outside of like, 1d12 Sidereals and a handful of gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Surely you mean 1d10, we don't use anything fancier than that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T15:58:11-07:00","id":1084740,"title":"","content":"I might be a specially oblivious guy, but I see no pretention whatsoever in the title. Not that I specially care anyways. If nothing, the flowery titles might make someone think about them more than the more straightforward ones of yetereditions. For good or bad, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T00:31:56-07:00","id":1084915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1082625-why-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-as-the-title?p=1084651#post1084651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the power of Names in 3e? Could removing her Name from every possible record be a form of protection from Sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it made her immune to people trying to dig up dirt in her family tree","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T05:40:09-07:00","id":1084980,"title":"","content":"The Scarlet Empress just doesn't want to be spammed by Infallible Messengers, cause you know, that sucks...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1550-angwe","name":"Angwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1550_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T11:20:43-07:00","id":1085083,"title":"","content":"Hmm... I'm not sure if the books ever make it explicit one way or the other, but I find the framing of the usual way we're told about the Scarlet Empress having been a minor officer of the Shogunate is a feature of the founding mythology of the Realm.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T11:35:12-07:00","id":1085089,"title":"","content":"Going by some of the other things we have gotten about Lookshy and the Tiger Generals, at the very least the Scarlet Empress was not a terribly important or famous figure prior to taking control control of the Sword of Creation because none of these people had heard of her before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T12:41:20-07:00","id":1085102,"title":"","content":"I agree. While her mastery of the Realm Defense Grid was strangely fortuitous, it could have just been someone yanking the threads of Fate until someone close enough and competent enough managed to get to the control panels. Since all of her companions were killed by the defenses of the control Manse, it would have been relatively easy for her to just not tell anyone her name in order to keep an air of mystery about her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-28T16:31:18-07:00","id":1085216,"title":"","content":"Honestly?<br /> <br /> I've always just figured that 'The Scarlet Empress' was her regnal name, but that her real one wasn't <i>secret</i> so much as obscure - known by and of interest to only historians studying the Shogunate and early-Realm periods, since her reign predated all but a literal handful of her subjects' lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T13:07:20-07:00","id":1085546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1082625-why-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-as-the-title?p=1085216#post1085216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly?<br /> <br /> I've always just figured that 'The Scarlet Empress' was her regnal name, but that her real one wasn't <i>secret</i> so much as obscure - known by and of interest to only historians studying the Shogunate and early-Realm periods, since her reign predated all but a literal handful of her subjects' lives.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agreed. I don't think the average Roman cared that Caesar Augustus' real name was Gaius Octavius during his reign, let alone decades or centuries after his death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T16:01:32-07:00","id":1085611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1082625-why-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-as-the-title?p=1085546#post1085546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed. I don't think the average Roman cared that Caesar Augustus' real name was Gaius Octavius during his reign, let alone decades or centuries after his death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Octavius constantly changed his name because names were important to the Roman people.<br /> <br /> When he was declared Caesar's heir, he changed his name to Gaius Julius Caesar because 'Octavius' was a plebeian name, and his origins would hurt his chances in politics. Unsurprisingly, his political rivals and critics referred to him as<i> Octavianus </i>while he was still alive. His humble origin and attempts to hide them by changing his name was source of political mockery.<br /> <br /> Under the name Gaius Julius Caesar, he gained the loyalty of Julius Caesar's former troops and inflamed public opinion against his assassins. In fact, he used that name for about two decades and didn't take up 'Augustus' until the death of Mark Antony, long after he'd become beloved of the people, started the second trimvurate, and branded 300 senators as outlaws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-29T17:43:13-07:00","id":1085631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hippokrene</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1082625-why-dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-as-the-title?p=1085611#post1085611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *snip*.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that's all super interesting. I just randomly grabbed a name that I knew was a title. Cool to know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-30T23:27:01-07:00","id":1086085,"title":"","content":"To be honest... I don't think many would care what Aspect the Empress has. That she is Dragon-Blooded is enough... and that she has given birth to the current Great Houses (and many former Houses) of various aspects is all that people would really care about. Even in the various houses that have a strong leaning to one Aspect, you find Dragon-Bloods of a different Aspect. The Aspect of one's parents doesn't determine which Aspect you express... and as such, one's Aspect doesn't really hold that much meaning beyond that one Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bFurthermore... it is likely in the nearly 800 years that the Empress has reigned (over twice the length of the typical Dragon-Blooded lifespan) that she has increased her power to the point where she can use any Aspect. True... in 2nd Ed, these tended to be high Essence charms to express other Aspects... but given the changes in 3rd Ed already, there is no reason to assume that this won't be possible too.<br /> <br /> \u200bIn the end, the Aspect the Empress is isn't likely to matter much in any game... even a Dragon-Blooded generational game from the early days of the Realm to the present. All that really matters is that the Empress is Dragon-Blooded... and in control of the most powerful device to ensure her rule. Beyond these facts... nothing else really matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}